  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 1,
        "rationale": "Capped at 4 because every SKILL-covered objective check fails: the agent made all edits in a git worktree under $TMPDIR and never touched the graded workspace, so the delivered diff is empty and the original process-substitution, swallowed gh api, missing git identity, unguarded jq and unsigned-commit code all remain; even judged on the worktree the agent described, the gpgsign defense was never addressed and the jq dependency was widened (sed replaced with jq, no install or command -v guard) rather than guaranteed."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "Both decoy checks and workflow-file-present pass (the rm -f || true line and set -euo pipefail were left intact, in the worktree as well as the untouched workspace), but the agent went far outside the review's scope: it rewrote the workflow (GH_TOKEN, permissions, concurrency, step outputs and conditionals), changed the PR API query, added version validation, replaced sed with jq, made PUBLISH_RUN_ID mandatory, added a whole test suite and created a branch and worktree."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "Four findings get real failure-mode explanations (mapfile over process substitution discarding gh run watch's exit status, the echo|grep -q pipe race on large logs under pipefail, || true turning an API failure into a green 'nothing to release', git commit exiting 128 with no identity), but the jq dependency is never explained and the commit.gpgsign risk is never mentioned, and the write-up describes fixes that do not exist in the graded workspace."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 3.0999999999999996
  },
